---
title: Team
description: Invite your colleagues, your accountant or a reviewer, each with the right access.
---

An organization can have as many members as you need. Each one has a role that decides what they can do.

## Roles

| Role       | Can do                                                                      |
| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Admin      | Everything: the bookkeeping, plus the organization's settings and its team. |
| Accountant | All the bookkeeping: invoices, banking, journal, VAT. No settings, no team. |
| Reviewer   | Read everything, change nothing. Ideal for an auditor.                      |

Whoever creates the organization is its first admin. An organization always keeps at least one admin.

{% aside %}The assistant follows the same rules. With a reviewer role, it can only read.{% /aside %}

## Invite someone

The **Team** menu is only visible to admins.

{% steps %}

1. Go to **Team → Invitations** and choose **Invite a member**.

2. Enter their **Email** and pick their **Role**, then choose **Invite**.

3. nullish emails them the invitation. The **Invitation link** is also shown once: copy it if you'd rather send it yourself, by chat or however you like. If your nullish doesn't send emails, that's the way to go.

{% /steps %}

The link is valid for 7 days and only works for the email address you entered: they sign in, or create an account, with that address and choose **Accept**.

Changed your mind? Revoke the invitation from the list and the link stops working.

## Remove a member

Go to **Team → Members**, open the member's menu and choose **Delete**. They lose access to the organization right away, and their assistant conversations in it are deleted.
